            "review_text": "Charlene2801\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam158 contributions\n0\nOver-priced and rude waiter!\nMar 2017 • Solo\nI visited the Trung Nguyen cafe on Nguyen Van Chiem st. D1 (opposite Diamond Plaza) today. It's a big cafe/restaurant with both outdoor and indoor areas. Usually with this size, they would have a hostess at the entrance to greet the guests and lead them to an appropriate table. Since the place is big, the guests wouldn't feel welcome if they have to walk in themselves. \n\nThey didn't have any hostess. I walked in and found myself a quiet corner with no greetings from any staff at all!. As I sat down, I told a waiter (obviously trying to avoid me because he was walking pass me. There was no way he didn't see me) that I needed a menu. He replied in a very rude way, didn't even turn his head to acknowledge me \"the menu is coming\" (in Vietnamese \"thực đơn sắp tới rồi kìa\") point to another waitress. \n\nThe waitress was fine. The food and drink were ok. However they were highly over-priced compared to their size and the cafe's location. I ordered a green tea latte jelly that costs 65000vnd and a bánh mì that costs 38000vnd. The size of the latte is half of the Starbucks/Coffee Bean/Phuc Long/Highland large size. And it costs the same! The bánh mi is so small with the same amount of meat as those at Highland (Highland's bánh mi are only 19000vnd/1). \n\nIn addition, other cafe would give you free flow of ice tea (trà đá) and paper tissue is always on the table. This Trung Nguyen cafe gives a small glass of ice tea (the staff was neglecting on giving me free flow as they were so near me and never came to check on my ice tea, and no tissue. You have to order the wet tissue separately! Even those road size bánh mi or street food shop would give you free wet tissue. The tissue is nothing to me. However it makes them seem so greedy. They just try to take as much as possible from the customers without giving adequate products and service! \n\nAs a Vietnamese, I'd always support Vietnamese brands. However, never Trung Nguyen cafe again. Wake up guys! If you want to market yourself as equal to Starbucks, get equal in quality and service too, not just the price! \n\nPlease see the pictures below to get a better idea of what I was talking about.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 31, 2017",
